OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FArgyll will be rather cloudy
OL,6,Fwith showers, occasionally heavy with
OL,7,Fa chance of thunder. Central Belt and
OL,8,Fsouth seeing bright spells with fewer
OL,9,Fshowers and more in the way of drier
OL,10,Fweather.
OL,11,
OL,12,CTonight:FBecoming mainly dry with
OL,13,Fclear periods this evening and
OL,14,Fovernight. A few showers continuing
OL,15,Facross Argyll and the Clyde coast
OL,16,Fthrough the night. Light winds.
OL,17,
OL,18,CFriday:FSome bright or sunny spells
OL,19,Fand a few well scattered showers,
OL,20,Falthough the south starting off dry.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
